From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] Support Chromium's ANGLE Vulkan backend and X11
 surfaces

ANGLE's ES 3.0 requirements are met: VK_EXT_provoking_vertex is advertised and
its structures are filtered before they reach the device,
standardSampleLocations is reported, and Wayland presentation support is
reported for queue family 0. Fence status is answered locally once a fence is
known to be signaled. vkMapMemory2/vkUnmapMemory2 use the socket shadow.
Dedicated allocations are not preferred for socket memory.

VK_KHR_xcb_surface creates a virtual surface bound to the X11 window, so X11
clients (Chromium under Xwayland) present through the same broker as Wayland
clients. Only one encoder may defer replies.
